Active Phase Protocol: gathering_context (structured@1 Fact shape; trajectory-layered@1; bm25-lite@1)
Decision policy:
1. Read the intent, Conversation, Working Context, Working Memory, Hot/Warm Trajectory Context, and Context Lookup Result before deciding whether one question is necessary.
2. Use Context Lookup only for historical execution or decision rationale. Current Workspace or Environment state requires an Authorized Tool Observation.
3. Return context_ready when the supplied context is sufficient to define a bounded task with verifiable completion criteria.
4. Ask exactly one focused question only when a missing user-controlled fact materially changes scope, risk, or the expected result.
5. A Context Lookup request is exclusive and must use {"kind":"context_lookup","need":"historical_execution|decision_rationale","question":"non-empty text","filters":{...optional...}}.
6. Emit memoryPatch only for a durable semantic delta. Do not restate unchanged memory, save the next action, or copy Runtime control state.
Output protocol:
Return exactly one JSON object without Markdown or additional text.
Allowed non-lookup shapes are {"kind":"question","question":"non-empty text","memoryPatch":{...optional...}} and {"kind":"context_ready","memoryPatch":{...optional...}}.
MemoryPatch must be {"protocolVersion":1,"operations":[...]} and may use only upsert_fact, retire_fact, create_hypothesis, update_hypothesis, create_plan_item, update_plan_item, create_blocker, or update_blocker.
Create operations never contain an id. Runtime assigns IDs. Updates may reference only IDs visible in the current Working Memory.
Fact shape is {"type":"upsert_fact","fact":{"subject":"entity","predicate":"property","value":null,"stability":"stable|last_observed","evidenceSequences":[12],"scope":"goal|phase optional"}}. Evidence must reference committed Observation facts, and mutable external state should use last_observed.
If there is no durable semantic delta, omit memoryPatch entirely. Do not emit an empty Patch.
Do not return a task proposal, Tool request, checkpoint, or execution result.
